{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nusing lint = long long;\nconst lint MOD = 1000000007;\n\ninline int add(int a, int b) {\n    a += b;\n    return a >= MOD ? a - MOD : a;\n}\n\ninline int sub(int a, int b) {\n    a -= b;\n    return a < 0 ? a + MOD : a;\n}\n\ninline lint mul(int a, int b) {\n    return (lint)a * b % MOD;\n}\n\nlint n;\nint k;\nvector<vector<int>> matmul(const vector<vector<int>>& A, const vector<vector<int>>& B) {\n    int sz = k + 1;\n    vector<vector<int>> C(sz, vector<int>(sz, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < sz; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < sz; ++j)\n            for (int t = 0; t < sz; ++t)\n                C[i][t] = add(C[i][t], (int)mul(A[i][j], B[j][t]));\n    return C;\n}\n\nvector<vector<vector<int>>> pref;\nvector<vector<int>> shift(const vector<vector<int>>& M) {\n    int sz = k + 1;\n    vector<vector<int>> R(sz, vector<int>(sz, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < sz; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < sz; ++j) {\n            int ni = i;\n            if (ni < k) ni = (ni + k - 1) % k;\n            int nj = j;\n            if (nj < k) nj = (nj + k - 1) % k;\n            R[i][j] = M[ni][nj];\n        }\n    return R;\n}\n\nvoid init() {\n    lint d = 0;\n    lint x = n;\n    while (x) { x /= k; ++d; }\n    pref.resize(d + 1);\n    pref[0].resize(k + 1, vector<int>(k + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i) pref[0][i][i] = 1;\n    pref[0][0][k] = 1;\n    pref[0][k][0] = MOD - 1;\n    pref[0][k][k] = 2;\n    \n    for (int s = 0; s < d; ++s) {\n        pref[s + 1] = pref[s];\n        auto cur = pref[s];\n        for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i) {\n            cur = shift(cur);\n            pref[s + 1] = matmul(pref[s + 1], cur);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvector<vector<int>> solve(lint x) {\n    if (x == 0) {\n        vector<vector<int>> I(k + 1, vector<int>(k + 1, 0));\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) I[i][i] = 1;\n        return I;\n    }\n    lint p = 1, d = 0;\n    while (p <= x / k) { p *= k; ++d; }\n    if (x == p) return pref[d];\n    lint steps = x / p;\n    lint rem = x - steps * p;\n    auto res = solve(0);\n    auto coef = pref[d];\n    for (lint i = 0; i < steps; ++i) {\n        res = matmul(res, coef);\n        coef = shift(coef);\n    }\n    auto other = solve(rem);\n    for (lint i = 0; i < steps; ++i) other = shift(other);\n    return matmul(res, other);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    init();\n    cout << solve(n)[k][k];\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    a += b\n    return a - MOD if a >= MOD else a\n\ndef sub(a, b):\n    a -= b\n    return a + MOD if a < 0 else a\n\ndef mul(a, b):\n    return (a * b) % MOD\n\ndef matmul(A, B, k):\n    sz = k + 1\n    C = [[0] * sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for i in range(sz):\n        for j in range(sz):\n            for t in range(sz):\n                C[i][t] = add(C[i][t], mul(A[i][j], B[j][t]))\n    return C\n\ndef shift(M, k):\n    sz = k + 1\n    R = [[0] * sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for i in range(sz):\n        for j in range(sz):\n            ni = i\n            if ni < k:\n                ni = (ni + k - 1) % k\n            nj = j\n            if nj < k:\n                nj = (nj + k - 1) % k\n            R[i][j] = M[ni][nj]\n    return R\n\ndef init(n, k):\n    d = 0\n    x = n\n    while x:\n        x //= k\n        d += 1\n    pref = [None] * (d + 1)\n    pref[0] = [[0] * (k + 1) for _ in range(k + 1)]\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        pref[0][i][i] = 1\n    pref[0][0][k] = 1\n    pref[0][k][0] = MOD - 1\n    pref[0][k][k] = 2\n    \n    for s in range(d):\n        pref[s + 1] = [row[:] for row in pref[s]]\n        cur = [row[:] for row in pref[s]]\n        for i in range(1, k):\n            cur = shift(cur, k)\n            pref[s + 1] = matmul(pref[s + 1], cur, k)\n    return pref\n\ndef solve(x, k, pref):\n    if x == 0:\n        I = [[0] * (k + 1) for _ in range(k + 1)]\n        for i in range(k + 1):\n            I[i][i] = 1\n        return I\n    p = 1\n    d = 0\n    while p <= x // k:\n        p *= k\n        d += 1\n    if x == p:\n        return pref[d]\n    steps = x // p\n    rem = x - steps * p\n    res = solve(0, k, pref)\n    coef = pref[d]\n    for i in range(steps):\n        res = matmul(res, coef, k)\n        coef = shift(coef, k)\n    other = solve(rem, k, pref)\n    for i in range(steps):\n        other = shift(other, k)\n    return matmul(res, other, k)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    pref = init(n, k)\n    result = solve(n, k, pref)\n    print(result[k][k])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001433984871255234, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.08749308437108994, -6.711257447022945e-05, 